      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 342 and 285. This is calculated by the formula: GCD(a, b) = GCD(b, a mod b).\n\nFor 342 and 285:\nGCD(342, 285) = GCD(285, 342 % 285) = GCD(285, 57) = GCD(57, 285 % 57) = GCD(57, 24) = GCD(24, 57 % 24) = GCD(24, 15) = GCD(15, 24 % 15) = GCD(15, 9) = GCD(9, 15 % 9) = GCD(9, 6) = GCD(6, 9 % 6) = GCD(6, 3) = GCD(3, 6 % 3) = GCD(3, 0) = 3\n\nTherefore, the largest common divisor of 342 and 285 is 3. $\\boxed{3}$",
